    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of what `POST /api/owners` does. The endpoint is defined by `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`, whose steps run in the sequence below. I've marked each as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutates state / derives data).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n0. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` on the whole file. Without that role the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 **[V]** Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already recorded, throws `IdempotentReplayException` to replay the original owner (200) instead of creating a new one. No key, or unseen key \u2192 continue.\n\n2. **`RequireDailyLimit`** \u2014 **[V]** Counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (today rolled to the next business day). At **\u2265 100** \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n3. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 this is the single `@RequestBody` binding (bound as `OwnerFieldsDto`, **not** `@Valid`, so no JSR-303 bean validation runs).\n   - **[S]** Computes the effective address: if `addressLine1` is non-blank, stores normalized `addressLine1` (+ space + normalized `addressLine2` when present); otherwise stores the normalized flat `address`. Written back onto the request.\n   - **[V]** Requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` all non-null/non-blank; any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n   - **[S]** Publishes the request as a variable for later steps.\n\n4. **`RequireValidPostcode`** \u2014 **[V]** If `postcode` is present it must be 4 digits, and for a city with a known region within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown region accepts any 4 digits. Absent postcode is allowed. Violation \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 **[S]** Rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place: strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`. **[V]** If the result isn't 8\u201315 digits after `+` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")` (400).\n\n6. **`ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`** \u2014 **[V]** Checks national-number length by country code: `+61` must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10. Wrong length \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")` (400).\n\n7. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 Optional email. If present: **[V]** must match the email regex, and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"email\")` (400); **[S]** stores it lower-cased in place. Absent email \u2192 untouched.\n\n*(Steps 8 onward all run under `govern: [ transaction ]` \u2014 one shared write transaction committed at the end.)*\n\n8. **`RequireUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 **[V]** Builds an identity key (`telephone | email | \"\"`) and compares against every non-deleted owner's key. Exact full-key match \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (409).\n\n9. **`RequireUniqueHousehold`** \u2014 **[V]** If `sharesHousehold` is true, or postcode is null/blank, skips. Otherwise computes household id (last name + postcode) and rejects if any non-deleted owner shares it \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (409).\n\n10. **`RequireCityCapacity`** \u2014 **[V]** Counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive). At **\u2265 50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n11. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 **[S]** Maps the request DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`. **[V]** If a supplied `registrationDate` is in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). **[S]** Defaults a missing date to today, then rolls the effective date forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 holidays). Publishes the built `Owner`.\n\n12. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 **[S]** Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over telephone+lastName), appending `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) on collision with an existing code.\n\n13. **`CountNamesakes`** \u2014 **[S]** Sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n14. **`CountHousehold`** \u2014 **[S]** Sets `householdCount` to existing household members (same last name + postcode) **plus one** (the new owner). Drives the GOLD tier.\n\n15. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 **[S]** If `sharesHousehold` is true, sets `possibleDuplicate=false`. Otherwise, if another owner shares last name + postcode (normalized) but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<that owner id>`; else `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n16. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 **[S]** Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n17. **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 **[S]** If an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, records the saved owner's DTO under that key for future replay.\n\n18. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 **[S]** Maps the owner to `OwnerDto` (deriving displayName, initials, telephoneDisplay, householdId, identityKey, checkDigit, membershipNumber/points/level, locality, timezone, contactPreference, ageBand, fiscalYear, selfLink, salutation, etc. via the mapper). **[S]** Sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` if more than 80 owners were created today. **[S]** Writes an `AUDIT` log line. Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body. The shared transaction commits here.\n\n**Notes**\n- The first three duplicate/limit checks that hit the DB (`RequireDailyLimit`, `RequireCityCapacity`, uniqueness scans) all use `ownerRepository.findAll()` and stream-filter in memory.\n- `RequireDailyLimit` (step 2) counts against `registrationDate`, but `BuildOwner` (step 11) can roll a weekend/holiday date forward, so the date counted at step 2 (based on `LocalDate.now()` rolled) and the date finally stored can be computed at different points \u2014 worth being aware of, but that's the code as written."
